{% comment %}
  Tungacea — Botanische Dokumentation (Produktseite).

  Rendered from sections/main-product.liquid via:
    {% render 'specimen-passport', product: product, block: block %}

  Everything here is composed from click values. The merchant selects from fixed
  lists and types nothing; this snippet turns those values into sentences, and
  because the values are fixed the sentences exist in every locale.

  A field left empty produces no line at all — no "unknown", no gap.

  Reads (all namespace `custom`):
  - lieferumfang    Auswahl  — what the buyer receives
  - mutterpflanze   Referenz — metaobject `mutterpflanze`
  - stadium         Auswahl
  - blaetter        Zahl
  - blattlaenge_cm  Zahl
  - bewurzelung     Auswahl  — also derives the experience hint
  - zuechter        Referenz — metaobject `person`
  - bezogen_von     Referenz — metaobject `person`
  - specimen_id     Text
  - aufnahmedatum   Datum

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} Product Liquid object (required)
  - block:   {Object} main-product `specimen` block (required)
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign mf = product.metafields.custom

  assign sp_lieferumfang = mf.lieferumfang.value | default: '' | strip
  assign sp_stadium = mf.stadium.value | default: '' | strip
  assign sp_bewurzelung = mf.bewurzelung.value | default: '' | strip
  assign sp_blaetter = mf.blaetter.value
  assign sp_blattlaenge = mf.blattlaenge_cm.value
  assign sp_id = mf.specimen_id.value | default: '' | strip
  assign sp_datum = mf.aufnahmedatum.value

  assign mutter = mf.mutterpflanze.value
  assign zuechter = mf.zuechter.value
  assign bezogen = mf.bezogen_von.value

  comment
    Lieferumfang decides the lead sentence, but the wording depends on whether a
    mother plant is actually shown further down. Pointing at a plant that is not
    there would be worse than saying nothing, so the kind is noted here and the
    sentence is built once the mother is resolved.

    An explicit case, not a translation key assembled at runtime: every key
    stays verifiable, and the stored values carry umlauts that would not
    survive being turned into a handle.
  endcomment
  assign delivery_kind = ''
  assign thing_word = ''
  case sp_lieferumfang
    when 'Dieses Exemplar'
      assign delivery_kind = 'exact'
      assign thing_word = 'products.product.specimen.thing_exact' | t
    when 'Cutting der Mutterpflanze'
      assign delivery_kind = 'cutting'
      assign thing_word = 'products.product.specimen.thing_cutting' | t
    when 'Sämling aus dieser Kreuzung'
      assign delivery_kind = 'seedling'
      assign thing_word = 'products.product.specimen.thing_seedling' | t
  endcase

  comment
    The experience hint is derived, never entered. It therefore cannot be
    forgotten on a product where it matters. Two parts so the opening can be
    set in bold without markup inside a translation string.
  endcomment
  assign rooting_label = ''
  assign hint_title = ''
  assign hint_body = ''
  case sp_bewurzelung
    when 'Unbewurzelt'
      assign rooting_label = 'products.product.specimen.rooting_none' | t
      assign hint_title = 'products.product.specimen.hint_unrooted_title' | t
      assign hint_body = 'products.product.specimen.hint_unrooted_body' | t
    when 'Frisch bewurzelt'
      assign rooting_label = 'products.product.specimen.rooting_fresh' | t
      assign hint_title = 'products.product.specimen.hint_fresh_title' | t
      assign hint_body = 'products.product.specimen.hint_fresh_body' | t
    when 'Etabliert bewurzelt'
      assign rooting_label = 'products.product.specimen.rooting_established' | t
  endcase

  assign stage_label = ''
  case sp_stadium
    when 'Steckling'
      assign stage_label = 'products.product.specimen.stage_cutting' | t
    when 'Sämling'
      assign stage_label = 'products.product.specimen.stage_seedling' | t
    when 'Jungpflanze'
      assign stage_label = 'products.product.specimen.stage_young' | t
    when 'Etabliert'
      assign stage_label = 'products.product.specimen.stage_established' | t
    when 'Mutterpflanze'
      assign stage_label = 'products.product.specimen.stage_mother' | t
  endcase

  comment
    Specs line: rooting, leaves, leaf length. Only the parts that exist. A leaf
    count of zero is a real value, so it is tested for nil and not for
    truthiness, which would swallow it.
  endcomment
  assign spec_parts = ''
  if rooting_label != blank
    assign spec_parts = spec_parts | append: rooting_label | append: '||'
  elsif stage_label != blank
    assign spec_parts = spec_parts | append: stage_label | append: '||'
  endif
  if sp_blaetter != nil
    assign leaves = 'products.product.specimen.leaves' | t: count: sp_blaetter
    assign spec_parts = spec_parts | append: leaves | append: '||'
  endif
  if sp_blattlaenge != nil
    assign leaflen = 'products.product.specimen.leaf_length' | t: cm: sp_blattlaenge
    assign spec_parts = spec_parts | append: leaflen | append: '||'
  endif
  assign spec_list = spec_parts | split: '||'

  comment
    Mother plant. The photo credit only appears when the photographer is
    somebody else — an empty `fotograf` means the picture is Tung's own.
  endcomment
  assign mutter_name = ''
  assign mutter_wo = ''
  assign mutter_credit = ''
  assign mutter_fotos = empty
  assign zeige_fotos = false
  if mutter != blank
    assign mutter_name = mutter.bezeichnung.value | default: '' | strip
    assign mutter_besitzer = mutter.besitzer.value
    if mutter_besitzer != blank
      assign besitzer_name = mutter_besitzer.instagram.value | default: mutter_besitzer.name.value | strip
    endif

    comment
      The line under the photos names the relationship, not just the address.
      Where the plant stands is a detail; that the offered plant comes from this
      one, and that this one is not for sale, is the point. Without a known
      Lieferumfang there is no relationship to state, so it falls back to the
      plain location.
    endcomment
    if thing_word != blank
      if besitzer_name != blank
        assign mutter_wo = 'products.product.specimen.mother_from_at' | t: thing: thing_word, who: besitzer_name
      else
        assign mutter_wo = 'products.product.specimen.mother_from_own' | t: thing: thing_word
      endif
    elsif besitzer_name != blank
      assign mutter_wo = 'products.product.specimen.mother_at' | t: who: besitzer_name
    else
      assign mutter_wo = 'products.product.specimen.mother_own' | t
    endif

    assign fotograf = mutter.fotograf.value
    if fotograf != blank
      assign fotograf_name = fotograf.instagram.value | default: fotograf.name.value | strip
      assign mutter_credit = 'products.product.specimen.photo_credit' | t: who: fotograf_name
    endif

    comment
      The permission gate. A photograph taken by somebody else is only shown
      when the permission switch is set on the mother plant entry. An empty
      photographer means the picture is Tung's own, so nothing to ask.
      Refusing to render is deliberate: a missing picture is a small problem, a
      borrowed one on a sales page is not.
    endcomment
    assign mutter_fotos = mutter.fotos.value
    if mutter_fotos.size > 0
      assign freigabe = mutter.bildfreigabe.value
      if fotograf == blank
        assign zeige_fotos = true
      elsif freigabe == true or freigabe == 'true'
        assign zeige_fotos = true
      endif
    endif
  endif

  comment
    The lead sentence, now that it is known whether a mother plant is shown.
    The old wording said a cutting came from the specimen pictured, which was a
    circle: the gallery shows what is being sold, so a cutting could not come
    from it. It now points at the mother plant, and only when there is one to
    point at.
  endcomment
  assign lead = ''
  case delivery_kind
    when 'exact'
      assign lead = 'products.product.specimen.delivery_exact' | t
    when 'cutting'
      if mutter_name != blank
        assign lead = 'products.product.specimen.delivery_cutting_mother' | t
      else
        assign lead = 'products.product.specimen.delivery_cutting_plain' | t
      endif
    when 'seedling'
      if mutter_name != blank
        assign lead = 'products.product.specimen.delivery_seedling_cross' | t
      else
        assign lead = 'products.product.specimen.delivery_seedling_plain' | t
      endif
  endcase

  assign zuechter_name = ''
  if zuechter != blank
    assign zuechter_name = zuechter.name.value | default: '' | strip
  endif
  assign bezogen_name = ''
  if bezogen != blank
    assign bezogen_name = bezogen.instagram.value | default: bezogen.name.value | strip
  endif

  assign has_lower = false
  if zuechter_name != blank or bezogen_name != blank or sp_id != blank
    assign has_lower = true
  endif

  comment
    The date format lives in the locale file. A German and an English reader do
    not write the same date the same way, so the pattern is translated too.
  endcomment
  assign datum_fmt = ''
  if sp_datum != nil
    assign date_pattern = 'products.product.specimen.date_format' | t
    assign datum_fmt = sp_datum | date: date_pattern
  endif

  assign has_anything = false
  if lead != blank or spec_list.size > 0 or mutter_name != blank or has_lower
    assign has_anything = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if has_anything -%}
  {{ 'component-specimen-passport.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

  <section
    class="specimen-passport quick-add-hidden"
    aria-labelledby="SpecimenPassport-title-{{ block.id }}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    <header class="specimen-passport__header">
      <div class="specimen-passport__heading-group">
        <p class="specimen-passport__eyebrow">{{ 'products.product.specimen.eyebrow' | t }}</p>
        <h2 class="specimen-passport__title" id="SpecimenPassport-title-{{ block.id }}">
          {{- 'products.product.specimen.heading' | t -}}
        </h2>
      </div>
    </header>

    {%- if lead != blank -%}
      <p class="specimen-passport__lead" data-testid="specimen-lead">
        <strong>{{ lead }}</strong>
        {%- if datum_fmt != blank %}
          {{ 'products.product.specimen.photographed_on' | t: date: datum_fmt }}
        {%- endif -%}
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if spec_list.size > 0 -%}
      <p class="specimen-passport__specs" data-testid="specimen-specs">
        {%- for part in spec_list -%}
          {{- part -}}{%- unless forloop.last %} · {% endunless -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      The mother plant follows the lead sentence directly, because that sentence
      points at her: the shorter the way to "shown below", the better it holds.
      The experience hint comes after her — it is a caveat, and a caveat placed
      second makes the whole record read like a warning.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if mutter_name != blank -%}
      <div class="specimen-passport__mother" data-testid="specimen-mother">
        <p class="specimen-passport__mother-label">{{ 'products.product.specimen.mother' | t }}</p>
        <p class="specimen-passport__mother-name">{{ mutter_name | escape }}</p>
        {%- if mutter_wo != blank -%}
          <p class="specimen-passport__mother-where">{{ mutter_wo }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          Portrait, like the product gallery, so a whole plant is visible at a
          glance instead of a cropped middle. The width and height attributes
          match that ratio, otherwise the page jumps while the images load.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if zeige_fotos -%}
          <script src="{{ 'specimen-lightbox.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
          <specimen-lightbox>
            <ul class="specimen-passport__mother-photos list-unstyled" role="list" data-testid="specimen-mother-photos">
              {%- for foto in mutter_fotos limit: 6 -%}
                <li>
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class="specimen-passport__mother-photo"
                    data-lightbox-full="{{ foto | image_url: width: 1800 }}"
                    data-lightbox-alt="{{ mutter_name | escape }}"
                    aria-label="{{ 'products.product.specimen.photo_open' | t: name: mutter_name }}"
                  >
                    <img
                      src="{{ foto | image_url: width: 480 }}"
                      srcset="{{ foto | image_url: width: 320 }} 320w, {{ foto | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w, {{ foto | image_url: width: 720 }} 720w"
                      sizes="(min-width: 750px) 18rem, 30vw"
                      alt=""
                      width="480"
                      height="600"
                      loading="lazy"
                    >
                  </button>
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>

            <dialog class="specimen-lightbox" aria-label="{{ mutter_name | escape }}">
              <button
                type="button"
                class="specimen-lightbox__close"
                data-lightbox-close
                aria-label="{{ 'products.product.specimen.photo_close' | t }}"
              >
                <span aria-hidden="true">&times;</span>
              </button>
              <img class="specimen-lightbox__image" data-lightbox-image src="" alt="">
            </dialog>
          </specimen-lightbox>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if mutter_credit != blank -%}
          <p class="specimen-passport__credit">{{ mutter_credit }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if has_lower -%}
      <dl class="specimen-passport__grid">
        {%- if zuechter_name != blank -%}
          <div class="specimen-passport__row">
            <dt class="specimen-passport__label">{{ 'products.product.specimen.breeder' | t }}</dt>
            <dd class="specimen-passport__value" data-testid="specimen-breeder">{{ zuechter_name | escape }}</dd>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if bezogen_name != blank -%}
          <div class="specimen-passport__row">
            <dt class="specimen-passport__label">{{ 'products.product.specimen.sourced' | t }}</dt>
            <dd class="specimen-passport__value" data-testid="specimen-sourced">{{ bezogen_name | escape }}</dd>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if sp_id != blank -%}
          <div class="specimen-passport__row">
            <dt class="specimen-passport__label">{{ 'products.product.specimen.id_label' | t }}</dt>
            <dd class="specimen-passport__value" data-testid="specimen-id">{{ sp_id | escape }}</dd>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </dl>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      The experience hint closes the record. Everything above it is what the
      specimen is and where it comes from; this is the one caveat, and a caveat
      belongs after the case it qualifies, not in front of it.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if hint_title != blank -%}
      <p class="specimen-passport__hint" role="note" data-testid="specimen-hint">
        <strong>{{ hint_title }}</strong> {{ hint_body }}
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </section>
{%- endif -%}
